abstract: "In the circular constant-friction model of fluid-driven aseismic slip, the slip-rate history at the injection point decides when full sliding is first lost: an instantaneous criterion for rise-then-fall rates, historical criteria for multi-peak and stepped rates under stated startup conditions, centre-first loss, and explicit consequences (drop tolerance, two-term finite-radius criterion, shut-in deadline, no linear taper halves the rate for a point source). Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text and data CC0-1.0; code MIT."
